      "gold_answer": "We can rewrite the summand as \\[\\begin{aligned} \\log_2\\left(1+\\frac1k\\right) \\log_k2\n\\log_{k+1}2 &= \\frac{ \\log_2\\left(\\frac{k+1}{k}\\right)}{\\log_2 k \\log_2 (k+1)} \\\\ &=\n\\frac{\\log_2(k+1) - \\log_2 k}{\\log_2 k \\log_2 (k+1)} \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{\\log_2 k} -\n\\frac{1}{\\log_2 (k+1)}. \\end{aligned}\\]Therefore, the sum telescopes: \\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{k=2}^{63} \\log_2\\left(1 + \\frac{1}{k}\\right) \\log_k 2 \\log_{k+1} 2 &=\n\\left(\\frac{1}{\\log_2 2} - \\frac{1}{\\log_2 3}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{\\log_2 3} -\n\\frac1{\\log_2 4}\\right) + \\dots + \\left(\\frac{1}{\\log_2 63} - \\frac{1}{\\log_2 64}\\right)\n\\\\ &= \\frac{1}{\\log_2 2} - \\frac{1}{\\log_2 64} \\\\ &= 1 - \\frac16 \\\\ &= \\boxed{\\frac56}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]",
